WEBVTT

00:00.240 --> 00:03.600
So now we're going to start with the big question how to build the server layer.

00:03.640 --> 00:04.840
What is the process.

00:04.880 --> 00:05.200
Okay.

00:05.240 --> 00:08.040
As usual first things first we have to analyze.

00:08.080 --> 00:13.120
And now the task before building anything in the server layer, we have to go and explore the data in

00:13.120 --> 00:15.800
order to understand the content of our sources.

00:15.800 --> 00:18.880
Once we have it, what we're going to do, we will be starting coding.

00:18.880 --> 00:21.920
And here the transformation that we're going to do is data cleansing.

00:21.920 --> 00:26.560
This is usually a process that takes really long time, and I usually do it in three steps.

00:26.560 --> 00:31.600
The first step is to check first the data quality issues that we have in the bronze layer.

00:31.600 --> 00:36.040
So before writing any data transformations, first we have to understand what are the issues.

00:36.040 --> 00:42.040
And only then I start writing data transformations in order to fix all those quality issues that we

00:42.040 --> 00:43.000
have in the bronze.

00:43.000 --> 00:47.560
And the last tip, once I have clean results, what we're going to do, we're going to go and insert

00:47.560 --> 00:49.080
it into the silver layer.

00:49.080 --> 00:53.920
And those are the three phases that we will be doing as we are writing the code for the silver layer.

00:53.920 --> 00:58.320
And the third step, once we have all the data in the silver layer, we have to make sure that the data

00:58.320 --> 01:01.600
is now correct and we don't have any quality issues anymore.

01:01.640 --> 01:03.360
And if you find any issues, Of course.

01:03.360 --> 01:05.360
What you're going to do, we're going to go back to coding.

01:05.360 --> 01:06.840
We're going to do the data cleansing.

01:06.840 --> 01:07.800
And again check.

01:07.800 --> 01:10.640
So it is like a cycle between validating and coding.

01:10.640 --> 01:16.280
Once the quality of the silver layer is good, we cannot skip the last phase where we're going to document

01:16.280 --> 01:17.960
and commit our work in the GitHub.

01:17.960 --> 01:20.240
And here we're going to have two new documentations.

01:20.240 --> 01:24.920
We're going to build the data flow diagram and as well the data integration diagram.

01:24.960 --> 01:29.040
After we understood the relationship between the sources from the first step.

01:29.040 --> 01:32.640
So this is the process and this is how we're going to build the server layer.

01:32.680 --> 01:33.040
All right.

01:33.040 --> 01:35.360
So now exploring the data in the bronze layer.

01:35.360 --> 01:40.880
So why it is very important because understanding the data it is the key to make smart decisions in

01:40.880 --> 01:41.680
the server layer.

01:41.720 --> 01:43.800
It was not the focus in the bronze layer.

01:43.840 --> 01:49.560
To understand the content of the data at all, we focused only how to get the data to the data warehouse.

01:49.560 --> 01:55.600
So that's why we have now to take a moment in order to explore and understand the tables, and as well

01:55.640 --> 01:56.680
how to connect them.

01:56.680 --> 01:58.960
What are the relationship between these tables?

01:58.960 --> 02:04.080
And it is very important, as you are learning about new source system is to create like some kind of

02:04.120 --> 02:05.080
documentation.

